// the workflow script, and with --write splices it into the tracked script. On batch 15's pattern
// (plan-15/manifest/check15.js), for the script with P-148's lines (dc06efbbc): node --check on the original and the
// spliced copy; both parsed as the body of an async function, as the Workflow harness parses them, their export made
// const (the coordinator skill's references/delegating.md: a script is checked by parsing it as an async function
// body); every line outside the block byte-identical; the block evaluated with the script's own load checks and
// scatter order; the rungs I and A, their fields, no rung bringing a gate step (testSpecData runs from climb batch
// 19's landed summary), no rung declaring a checker count, a crash, landsOnlyWith or a ladder move; each section
// equal to the rung's section 3 of the record (backticks dropped, the ellipsis character as three full stops);
// briefing, reasons and checks equal to lists20.py's, one reason per key, checks a sub-list of the briefing; the
// two rungs outside the checker, A's test the stage and I's not, each section stating the distance stage, the count
// stage and no speed pass; no backtick or non-ASCII
// character in any string the agents read; no text asking a skeptic to see a failure again or a stage re-run without
// a code change (the coordinator skill's references/batch.md, "The workflow"); no LEDGER_FROM (the gather numbers
// rows through ledger.py); the record holding no copy of the block. Its last lines say whether the tracked script's
// block equals the generated one, and count the problems.
//   node check20.js [--write] [RECORD]      RECORD defaults to explorations/coordinator/CLIMB-BATCH-20.md
